  "limitations": [
    "Cooperative step/take driver, no background capture workers, real-time rate control, GPU inference, async scheduler or physical camera SDK.",
    "All pixels, timestamps and counts are synthetic; synchronized metadata is not measured hardware synchronization or factory throughput.",
    "No persistent queue, crash recovery, consumer acknowledgement/retry or exactly-once inference guarantee. Caller owns successfully taken bundles.",
    "Queue capacity counts four-lane bundles; one extra pending bundle is explicitly retained and reported, never silently overwritten.",
    "Forward-only scan, uniform lane width and finite source; stop/error preserves accepted prefix, not future unacquired lines.",
    "No seam/duplicate merging (Phase 14), no runtime profiling/async scheduling (Phase 15), no physical-unit QC rules.",
    "Phase 12 mapping still requires explicit coherent row-pitch/encoder calibration and exact geometry; short final chunks are not padded or relabelled as full-height calibrated images.",
    "Simulation IDs must identify the run configuration; IDs are deterministic camera/frame scoped, not global production idempotency keys."
  ]
